ICMP KEY TAKEAWAYS:
	ICMP doesn't happen automatically - you must trigger it 
	Ping uses Echo Request (Type 8) and Echo Reply (Type 0) 
	TTL shows how many hops between you and the target      
	Sequence numbers help identify lost packets             
	RTT (round trip time) shows network latency            
	Your PC ALWAYS talks to your router FIRST (MAC address)

How to Test ICMP Right Now:
	Step 1: Open Command Prompt
•	Press Windows Key + R
•	Type cmd and press Enter
	Step 2: Start Wireshark Capture
•	Click the blue shark fin to start capturing
•	Filter: icmp (just type it and press Enter)

	Step 3: Run Ping Commands
•	In the Command Prompt, type:
o	ping google.com
o	ping 8.8.8.8
o	ping 333.333.33.3 (your router)
Step 4: Look in Wireshark
•	You should see:
o	Echo (ping) request → Your PC asking "Are you there?"
o	Echo (ping) reply → The target answering "Yes, I'm here!"

 
